            {
                "entry_id": "bbb84249-7912-3279-be6a-2c2252e8a75f",
                "word": "Cockney",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "5a39d6e4-6bcb-432e-8bc6-9d1f1bb68c2d",
                        "entry_id": "bbb84249-7912-3279-be6a-2c2252e8a75f",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "Cockneys"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9d9cf251-d605-3e8f-9c22-cfb7c5b53602",
                        "entry_id": "bbb84249-7912-3279-be6a-2c2252e8a75f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Any Londoner."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "UK",
                            "slang"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "01518c70-b316-4d76-8ca0-369d625e1e3f",
                                "sense_id": "9d9cf251-d605-3e8f-9c22-cfb7c5b53602",
                                "text": "COCKNEY, a native of London. An ancient nickname implying effeminacy, used by the oldest English writers, and derived from the imaginary fool's paradise, or lubberland, Cockaygne."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3fc69686-f40a-360b-80c7-833def5b8ed2",
                        "entry_id": "bbb84249-7912-3279-be6a-2c2252e8a75f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A Londoner born within earshot of the city's Bow Bells, or (now generically) any working-class Londoner."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "UK"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "dccdc369-f8a3-4ac5-9493-3249ada65e2f",
                                "sense_id": "3fc69686-f40a-360b-80c7-833def5b8ed2",
                                "text": "Londoners, and all within the sound of Bow Bell, are in reproach called Cockneys."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e70d172b-7071-4cd4-be40-fa1e094c5fcb",
                                "sense_id": "3fc69686-f40a-360b-80c7-833def5b8ed2",
                                "text": "A Cockney or Cocksie, applied only to one born within the sound of Bow bell, that is in the City of London."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "97b50d34-aa6e-42e8-8311-4841d5fa93a5",
                                "sense_id": "3fc69686-f40a-360b-80c7-833def5b8ed2",
                                "text": "“Charming place, ma’am,” said he, bowing to the widow; “noble prospect—delightful to us Cocknies, who seldom see anything but Pall Mall.”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "53e123c3-09b7-4f5f-a4c3-5d0905f5299d",
                                "sense_id": "3fc69686-f40a-360b-80c7-833def5b8ed2",
                                "text": "Parkinson: You made films before, but the part that really made your name was Zulu, wasn't it […] and there of course—against type—you played the toff, you played the officer.\nCaine: I played the officer, yeah, and everybody thought I was like that. Everyone was so shocked when they met me, this like Cockney guy had played this toffee-nosed git."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "2a33ca7e-654d-36e6-84cb-30858cb31cac",
                "word": "cockney",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "b7f60740-992e-4d06-823b-1de243706386",
                        "entry_id": "2a33ca7e-654d-36e6-84cb-30858cb31cac",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "cockneys"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b971c5c1-6f60-3fd6-89dd-6b34ff5db2bb",
                        "entry_id": "2a33ca7e-654d-36e6-84cb-30858cb31cac",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A native or inhabitant of parts of the East End of London."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3bc64975-69b0-4d1e-b452-966bdf9b4c05",
                                "sense_id": "b971c5c1-6f60-3fd6-89dd-6b34ff5db2bb",
                                "text": "A cockney in a rural village was stared at as much as if he had entered a kraal of Hottentots."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a45e246f-bd46-392a-80ed-cca18d8693ba",
                        "entry_id": "2a33ca7e-654d-36e6-84cb-30858cb31cac",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An effeminate person; a spoilt child."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c5cc321f-6269-47f3-8fd0-778771ed7cb0",
                                "sense_id": "a45e246f-bd46-392a-80ed-cca18d8693ba",
                                "text": "A young heir, or cockney, that is his mother's darling[…]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a127cba4-bd06-4756-8719-fda48176f506",
                                "sense_id": "a45e246f-bd46-392a-80ed-cca18d8693ba",
                                "text": "This great lubber, the world, will prove a cockney."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
